WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.479
Build your own ride, one set at a time.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.989
Pick Intervals. Every set, the warm-up and the cool-down has its own times, levels

00:00:12.989 --> 00:00:14.263
and cadence aim.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.719
It starts with Descending recoveries: a five-minute warm-up, then five sets of

00:00:22.719 --> 00:00:25.681
thirty-second efforts at level twenty-eight.

00:00:25.881 --> 00:00:29.466
The recoveries shrink from three minutes to none, then a cool-down.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.265
The preview adds it up: thirty minutes.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.776
Edit opens a dialog. Give set two a third round, and save.

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:46.865
The row and the total follow: thirty-three minutes.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.424
The warm-up and the cool-down have their own dialog, and a switch to leave them out.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.123
Add set copies the last one. Move a set up or down, or remove it.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.700
Or start from Even sets: three sets of four efforts, seventeen minutes in all.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.239
On a phone, every row keeps its actions within reach.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.257
What the tests prove: a plan holds at most thirty efforts and a hundred and eighty

00:01:32.257 --> 00:01:32.972
minutes.

00:01:33.172 --> 00:01:36.862
And the last Intervals plan you started comes back after a reload.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.504
That is journey five. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.811
training display.
